IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `uc-core`
IMPORT `uc-core-persons`
IMPORT `uc2-part6-ch2-earned-income`

-- Tests of Part 6, Chapter 2, regulations 52 to 56, 60 and 61 (earned income, employed earnings, notional earned income,
-- real time information). Every expected value is worked out by hand from the text and written beside the assertion.

§ `Fixtures`

GIVEN payment IS A BOOLEAN
      volunteer IS A BOOLEAN
      `only expenses` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Work done by a person`
`test work` payment volunteer `only expenses` MEANS
    `Work done by a person` WITH
        `work is done for payment or in expectation of payment` IS payment
        `person is engaged by a charitable or voluntary organisation, or as a volunteer` IS volunteer
        `payment received or due to be paid is only in respect of expenses` IS `only expenses`

`test paid work` MEANS `test work` TRUE FALSE FALSE
`test volunteering for expenses` MEANS `test work` TRUE TRUE TRUE
`test unpaid work` MEANS `test work` FALSE FALSE FALSE

GIVEN a IS A BOOLEAN
      b IS A BOOLEAN
      c IS A BOOLEAN
      d IS A BOOLEAN
      e IS A BOOLEAN
      f IS A BOOLEAN
      g IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Person who may be participating as a service user`
`test service user` a b c d e f g MEANS
    `Person who may be participating as a service user` WITH
        `consulted by or on behalf of a body which has a statutory duty to provide services in the field of health, social care or social housing` IS a
        `consulted by or on behalf of a body which conducts research or undertakes monitoring for the purpose of planning or improving such services` IS b
        `consulted in their capacity as a user, potential user, carer of a user or person otherwise affected by the provision of those services` IS c
        `consulted by or on behalf of the Secretary of State in relation to the Secretary of State's functions in the field of social security or child support or under section 2 of the Employment and Training Act 1973` IS d
        `consulted by or on behalf of a body which conducts research or undertakes monitoring for the purpose of planning or improving such functions` IS e
        `consulted in their capacity as a person affected or potentially affected by the exercise of those functions or the carer of such a person` IS f
        `the carer of a person consulted under sub-paragraph (a) or (ab)` IS g

`test not a service user` MEANS `test service user` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
`test a service user` MEANS `test service user` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE

§ `Regulation 52 -- earned income`

GIVEN employment IS A BOOLEAN
      trade IS A BOOLEAN
      derived IS A BOOLEAN
      work IS A `Work done by a person`
      treated IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH AN `Income considered under regulation 52`
`test income` employment trade derived work treated MEANS
    `Income considered under regulation 52` WITH
        `remuneration or profits derived from employment under a contract of service or in an office, including elective office` IS employment
        `remuneration or profits derived from a trade, profession or vocation` IS trade
        `income derived from work done by the person` IS derived
        `work from which the income is derived` IS work
        `income treated as earned income in accordance with this Chapter` IS treated

#ASSERT `reg 52 — income is earned income` (`test income` TRUE FALSE FALSE `test unpaid work` FALSE)
#ASSERT `reg 52 — income is earned income` (`test income` FALSE TRUE FALSE `test unpaid work` FALSE)
#ASSERT `reg 52 — income is earned income` (`test income` FALSE FALSE TRUE `test paid work` FALSE)
#ASSERT `reg 52 — income is earned income` (`test income` FALSE FALSE FALSE `test unpaid work` TRUE)
-- Work done as a volunteer for expenses only is not paid work, so the income from it is not earned income under (a)(iii).
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 52 — income is earned income` (`test income` FALSE FALSE TRUE `test volunteering for expenses` FALSE))
-- Unpaid work: no.
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 52 — income is earned income` (`test income` FALSE FALSE TRUE `test unpaid work` FALSE))
-- Income from paid work that is not derived from it: no.
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 52 — income is earned income` (`test income` FALSE FALSE FALSE `test paid work` FALSE))
-- Nothing at all: no.
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 52 — income is earned income` (`test income` FALSE FALSE FALSE `test unpaid work` FALSE))

§ `Regulation 53(2) -- participating as a service user`

-- (a): a body with a statutory duty (or a research body) consults the person as a user.
#ASSERT `reg 53(2) — the person is participating as a service user` (`test service user` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT `reg 53(2) — the person is participating as a service user` (`test service user` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
-- Consulted by such a body, but not in the capacity of a user or affected person: no.
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 53(2) — the person is participating as a service user` (`test service user` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE))
-- The capacity without any consulting body: no.
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 53(2) — the person is participating as a service user` (`test service user` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE))
-- (ab): the Secretary of State consults the person as an affected person.
#ASSERT `reg 53(2) — the person is participating as a service user` (`test service user` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT `reg 53(2) — the person is participating as a service user` (`test service user` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 53(2) — the person is participating as a service user` (`test service user` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE))
-- The capacity of (ab) does not combine with the body of (a), or the capacity of (a) with the body of (ab).
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 53(2) — the person is participating as a service user` (`test service user` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE))
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 53(2) — the person is participating as a service user` (`test service user` FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE))
-- (b): the carer of a person consulted.
#ASSERT `reg 53(2) — the person is participating as a service user` (`test service user` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 53(2) — the person is participating as a service user` `test not a service user`)

§ `Regulation 54 -- general principles`

`test first-period determination` MEANS `Determination that may be based on an estimate` WITH
    `determination of whether the financial conditions in section 5 of the Act are met, made before the expiry of the first assessment period in relation to a claim` IS TRUE
    `determination of the amount of the person's earned income for an assessment period, where the person has failed to report information in relation to that earned income` IS FALSE
`test failed-to-report determination` MEANS `Determination that may be based on an estimate` WITH
    `determination of whether the financial conditions in section 5 of the Act are met, made before the expiry of the first assessment period in relation to a claim` IS FALSE
    `determination of the amount of the person's earned income for an assessment period, where the person has failed to report information in relation to that earned income` IS TRUE
`test ordinary determination` MEANS `Determination that may be based on an estimate` WITH
    `determination of whether the financial conditions in section 5 of the Act are met, made before the expiry of the first assessment period in relation to a claim` IS FALSE
    `determination of the amount of the person's earned income for an assessment period, where the person has failed to report information in relation to that earned income` IS FALSE

#ASSERT `reg 54(2) — the determination may be based on an estimate` `test first-period determination`
#ASSERT `reg 54(2) — the determination may be based on an estimate` `test failed-to-report determination`
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 54(2) — the determination may be based on an estimate` `test ordinary determination`)
-- (1): actual amounts received, 1,500; where an estimate is allowed and made (1,700), the estimate stands; allowed but not made, the actual amounts.
#ASSERT `reg 54(1) — the amounts on which the earned income for an assessment period is based` `test ordinary determination` 1500 NOTHING EQUALS 1500
#ASSERT `reg 54(1) — the amounts on which the earned income for an assessment period is based` `test ordinary determination` 1500 (JUST 1700) EQUALS 1500
#ASSERT `reg 54(1) — the amounts on which the earned income for an assessment period is based` `test first-period determination` 1500 (JUST 1700) EQUALS 1700
#ASSERT `reg 54(1) — the amounts on which the earned income for an assessment period is based` `test failed-to-report determination` 1500 (JUST 1700) EQUALS 1700
#ASSERT `reg 54(1) — the amounts on which the earned income for an assessment period is based` `test failed-to-report determination` 1500 NOTHING EQUALS 1500

§ `Regulation 55 -- employed earnings`

GIVEN benefit IS A Benefit
      amount IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `Payment of a benefit`
`test benefit payment` benefit amount MEANS
    `Payment of a benefit` WITH benefit IS benefit, amount IS amount

GIVEN general IS A NUMBER
      code IS A NUMBER
      exempt IS A NUMBER
      allowed IS A NUMBER
      svc IS A NUMBER
      participation IS A `Person who may be participating as a service user`
      benefits IS A LIST OF `Payment of a benefit`
      repayment IS A NUMBER
      work IS A `Work done by a person`
      selfemployed IS A BOOLEAN
      pension IS A NUMBER
      tax IS A NUMBER
      giving IS A NUMBER
GIVETH AN `Amounts received from an employment in an assessment period`
`test amounts` general code exempt allowed svc participation benefits repayment work selfemployed pension tax giving MEANS
    `Amounts received from an employment in an assessment period` WITH
        `general earnings as defined in section 7(3) of ITEPA` IS general
        `of which amounts treated as earnings under Chapters 2 to 11 of Part 3 of ITEPA (the benefits code)` IS code
        `of which amounts exempt from income tax under Part 4 of ITEPA` IS exempt
        `of which expenses allowed to be deducted under Chapter 2 of Part 5 of ITEPA` IS allowed
        `of which expenses arising from participation as a service user` IS svc
        `service user participation of the person` IS participation
        `benefits received` IS benefits
        `repayment of income tax or national insurance contributions received from HMRC in respect of a tax year` IS repayment
        `work done by the person in that tax year` IS work
        `the repayment is taken into account as self-employed earnings under regulation 57(4)` IS selfemployed
        `relievable pension contributions made by the person in the assessment period` IS pension
        `amounts paid by the person in the assessment period in respect of the employment by way of income tax or primary Class 1 contributions` IS tax
        `sums withheld as donations to an approved scheme under Part 12 of ITEPA (payroll giving)` IS giving

`test only general earnings` general MEANS
    `test amounts` general 0 0 0 0 `test not a service user` (EMPTY) 0 `test unpaid work` FALSE 0 0 0

#ASSERT `reg 55 — the employed earnings for an assessment period` (`test only general earnings` 2000) EQUALS 2000
-- (2): less amounts treated as earnings under the benefits code (300) and exempt amounts (200): 1,500.
#ASSERT `reg 55 — the employed earnings for an assessment period` (`test amounts` 2000 300 200 0 0 `test not a service user` (EMPTY) 0 `test unpaid work` FALSE 0 0 0) EQUALS 1500
-- (3)(a): expenses allowed under Chapter 2 of Part 5 of ITEPA (100) are disregarded: 1,900.
#ASSERT `reg 55 — the employed earnings for an assessment period` (`test amounts` 2000 0 0 100 0 `test not a service user` (EMPTY) 0 `test unpaid work` FALSE 0 0 0) EQUALS 1900
-- (3)(b): service-user expenses (50) are disregarded only if the person is a service user.
#ASSERT `reg 55 — the employed earnings for an assessment period` (`test amounts` 2000 0 0 0 50 `test a service user` (EMPTY) 0 `test unpaid work` FALSE 0 0 0) EQUALS 1950
#ASSERT `reg 55 — the employed earnings for an assessment period` (`test amounts` 2000 0 0 0 50 `test not a service user` (EMPTY) 0 `test unpaid work` FALSE 0 0 0) EQUALS 2000
-- (4): statutory sick pay 100 and statutory maternity pay 200 count; carer's allowance 50 does not: 300.
#ASSERT `reg 55 — the employed earnings for an assessment period` (`test amounts` 0 0 0 0 0 `test not a service user` (LIST `test benefit payment` `statutory sick pay` 100, `test benefit payment` `statutory maternity pay` 200, `test benefit payment` `carer's allowance` 50) 0 `test unpaid work` FALSE 0 0 0) EQUALS 300
-- All seven benefits listed: 10 + 20 + 30 + 40 + 50 + 60 + 70 = 280; employment and support allowance (500) is not listed.
#ASSERT `reg 55 — the employed earnings for an assessment period` (`test amounts` 0 0 0 0 0 `test not a service user` (LIST `test benefit payment` `statutory sick pay` 10, `test benefit payment` `statutory maternity pay` 20, `test benefit payment` `statutory paternity pay` 30, `test benefit payment` `statutory adoption pay` 40, `test benefit payment` `statutory shared parental pay` 50, `test benefit payment` `statutory parental bereavement pay` 60, `test benefit payment` `statutory neonatal care pay` 70, `test benefit payment` `employment and support allowance` 500) 0 `test unpaid work` FALSE 0 0 0) EQUALS 280
#ASSERT `reg 55(4) — a benefit treated as employed earnings` `statutory sick pay`
#ASSERT `reg 55(4) — a benefit treated as employed earnings` `statutory neonatal care pay`
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 55(4) — a benefit treated as employed earnings` `maternity allowance`)
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 55(4) — a benefit treated as employed earnings` `jobseeker's allowance`)
-- (4A): a repayment from HMRC (120) for a tax year in which the person was in paid work: counted; counted as self-employed earnings instead: not; not paid work: not.
#ASSERT `reg 55 — the employed earnings for an assessment period` (`test amounts` 0 0 0 0 0 `test not a service user` (EMPTY) 120 `test paid work` FALSE 0 0 0) EQUALS 120
#ASSERT `reg 55 — the employed earnings for an assessment period` (`test amounts` 0 0 0 0 0 `test not a service user` (EMPTY) 120 `test paid work` TRUE 0 0 0) EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `reg 55 — the employed earnings for an assessment period` (`test amounts` 0 0 0 0 0 `test not a service user` (EMPTY) 120 `test unpaid work` FALSE 0 0 0) EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `reg 55 — the employed earnings for an assessment period` (`test amounts` 0 0 0 0 0 `test not a service user` (EMPTY) 120 `test volunteering for expenses` FALSE 0 0 0) EQUALS 0
-- (5): pension contributions 100, income tax and Class 1 contributions 200 and payroll giving 10 come off 2,000: 1,690.
#ASSERT `reg 55 — the employed earnings for an assessment period` (`test amounts` 2000 0 0 0 0 `test not a service user` (EMPTY) 0 `test unpaid work` FALSE 100 200 10) EQUALS 1690
-- All together: 3000 - 500 - 100 = 2400; less disregarded 50 + 20 = 2330; plus SSP 100 = 2430; plus repayment 80 = 2510; less 150 + 300 + 5 = 455 gives 2055.
#ASSERT `reg 55 — the employed earnings for an assessment period` (`test amounts` 3000 500 100 50 20 `test a service user` (LIST `test benefit payment` `statutory sick pay` 100) 80 `test paid work` FALSE 150 300 5) EQUALS 2055
-- The result is not floored at nil (fork F-E1): 100 less 250 of tax is -150.
#ASSERT `reg 55 — the employed earnings for an assessment period` (`test amounts` 100 0 0 0 0 `test not a service user` (EMPTY) 0 `test unpaid work` FALSE 0 250 0) EQUALS (0 MINUS 150)
-- Regulation 6(1): 100.005 rounds to 100.01 and 100.004 to 100.
#ASSERT `reg 55 — the employed earnings for an assessment period` (`test only general earnings` 100.005) EQUALS 100.01
#ASSERT `reg 55 — the employed earnings for an assessment period` (`test only general earnings` 100.004) EQUALS 100

§ `Regulation 56 -- employee involved in a trade dispute`

GIVEN had IS A BOOLEAN
      withdrawn IS A BOOLEAN
      terminated IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH AN `Employee involved in a trade dispute`
`test employee` had withdrawn terminated MEANS
    `Employee involved in a trade dispute` WITH
        `the person has had employed earnings` IS had
        `the person has withdrawn their labour in furtherance of a trade dispute` IS withdrawn
        `the person's contract of service has been terminated` IS terminated
        `employed earnings the person would have had were it not for the trade dispute` IS 1500
        `employed earnings the person has` IS 0

-- Assumed at the level they would have had (1,500) when all three conditions are met.
#ASSERT `reg 56 — the employed earnings assumed for an employee involved in a trade dispute` (`test employee` TRUE TRUE FALSE) EQUALS 1500
-- Contract terminated, no withdrawal of labour, or no employed earnings before: the actual (nil).
#ASSERT `reg 56 — the employed earnings assumed for an employee involved in a trade dispute` (`test employee` TRUE TRUE TRUE) EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `reg 56 — the employed earnings assumed for an employee involved in a trade dispute` (`test employee` TRUE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `reg 56 — the employed earnings assumed for an employee involved in a trade dispute` (`test employee` FALSE TRUE FALSE) EQUALS 0

§ `Regulation 60 -- notional earned income`

GIVEN self IS A BOOLEAN
      employer IS A BOOLEAN
      purpose IS A BOOLEAN
      result IS A BOOLEAN
      opinion IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Deprivation of earned income`
`test deprivation` self employer purpose result opinion MEANS
    `Deprivation of earned income` WITH
        `amount of the earned income of which the person has been deprived` IS 5000
        `the person has deprived themselves of earned income` IS self
        `the person's employer has arranged for the person to be deprived of earned income` IS employer
        `the deprivation was for the purpose of securing entitlement to universal credit or to an increased amount of universal credit` IS purpose
        `entitlement or higher entitlement to universal credit did in fact result` IS result
        `in the opinion of the Secretary of State this was a foreseeable and intended consequence of the deprivation` IS opinion

-- (2): entitlement resulted and the Secretary of State thinks it was foreseeable and intended: the purpose is treated as existing.
#ASSERT `reg 60(2) — the purpose is treated as existing` (`test deprivation` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 60(2) — the purpose is treated as existing` (`test deprivation` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE))
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 60(2) — the purpose is treated as existing` (`test deprivation` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE))
-- (1): the person deprived themselves for the purpose: treated as possessing 5,000.
#ASSERT `reg 60(1) — the earned income the person is treated as possessing` (`test deprivation` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS 5000
-- The employer arranged it, and the purpose is treated as existing under (2): 5,000.
#ASSERT `reg 60(1) — the earned income the person is treated as possessing` (`test deprivation` FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE) EQUALS 5000
-- Deprived, but no purpose and (2) does not apply: nothing.
#ASSERT `reg 60(1) — the earned income the person is treated as possessing` (`test deprivation` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE) EQUALS 0
-- A purpose but nobody deprived them of anything: nothing.
#ASSERT `reg 60(1) — the earned income the person is treated as possessing` (`test deprivation` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS 0

GIVEN paid IS A NUMBER
      comparable IS A NUMBER
      means IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Services provided by a person for another person`
`test services` paid comparable means MEANS
    `Services provided by a person for another person` WITH
        `payment the other person makes for those services` IS paid
        `amount that would be paid for comparable services in the same location` IS comparable
        `the means of the other person were sufficient to pay for, or pay more for, those services` IS means
        `remuneration that would be reasonable for the provision of those services` IS 8000

GIVEN charity IS A BOOLEAN
      satisfied IS A BOOLEAN
      participation IS A `Person who may be participating as a service user`
      programme IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Services to which regulation 60(3) may not apply`
`test exceptions` charity satisfied participation programme MEANS
    `Services to which regulation 60(3) may not apply` WITH
        `the person is engaged to provide the services by a charitable or voluntary organisation` IS charity
        `the Secretary of State is satisfied that it is reasonable to provide the services free of charge or at less than the rate that would be paid for comparable services in the same location` IS satisfied
        `service user participation of the person` IS participation
        `the services are provided under or in connection with a person's participation in an employment or training programme approved by the Secretary of State` IS programme

`test no exception` MEANS `test exceptions` FALSE FALSE `test not a service user` FALSE

-- (3): no payment, or less than the comparable payment, where the other person could afford more: reasonable remuneration (8,000).
#ASSERT `reg 60(3) — the remuneration the person is treated as having received` (`test services` 0 10000 TRUE) `test no exception` EQUALS JUST 8000
#ASSERT `reg 60(3) — the remuneration the person is treated as having received` (`test services` 5000 10000 TRUE) `test no exception` EQUALS JUST 8000
-- A payment equal to or above the comparable payment: paragraph (3) does not apply.
#ASSERT `reg 60(3) — the remuneration the person is treated as having received` (`test services` 10000 10000 TRUE) `test no exception` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `reg 60(3) — the remuneration the person is treated as having received` (`test services` 12000 10000 TRUE) `test no exception` EQUALS NOTHING
-- The other person's means were not sufficient: it does not apply.
#ASSERT `reg 60(3) — the remuneration the person is treated as having received` (`test services` 0 10000 FALSE) `test no exception` EQUALS NOTHING
-- (4)(a): a charity engages them and the Secretary of State is satisfied: excepted. A charity but no satisfaction: not excepted.
#ASSERT `reg 60(3) — the remuneration the person is treated as having received` (`test services` 0 10000 TRUE) (`test exceptions` TRUE TRUE `test not a service user` FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `reg 60(3) — the remuneration the person is treated as having received` (`test services` 0 10000 TRUE) (`test exceptions` TRUE FALSE `test not a service user` FALSE) EQUALS JUST 8000
#ASSERT `reg 60(3) — the remuneration the person is treated as having received` (`test services` 0 10000 TRUE) (`test exceptions` FALSE TRUE `test not a service user` FALSE) EQUALS JUST 8000
-- (4)(b): participating as a service user: excepted.
#ASSERT `reg 60(3) — the remuneration the person is treated as having received` (`test services` 0 10000 TRUE) (`test exceptions` FALSE FALSE `test a service user` FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
-- (4)(c): an approved programme: excepted.
#ASSERT `reg 60(3) — the remuneration the person is treated as having received` (`test services` 0 10000 TRUE) (`test exceptions` FALSE FALSE `test not a service user` TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Regulation 61 -- information; real time information`

#ASSERT `reg 61(1) — the person must provide the information for calculating their earned income` TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 61(1) — the person must provide the information for calculating their earned income` TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 61(1) — the person must provide the information for calculating their earned income` FALSE FALSE)

GIVEN rti IS A BOOLEAN
      a IS A BOOLEAN
      b IS A BOOLEAN
      c IS A BOOLEAN
      reported IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH AN `Employment considered under regulation 61`
`test employment` rti a b c reported MEANS
    `Employment considered under regulation 61` WITH
        `the employer is a Real Time Information employer` IS rti
        `the Secretary of State considers that the employer is unlikely to report information to HMRC in a sufficiently accurate or timely manner` IS a
        `it appears to the Secretary of State that the amount of a payment reported to HMRC is incorrect, or fails to reflect the definition of employed earnings in regulation 55 in some material respect` IS b
        `no information is received from HMRC in the assessment period and the Secretary of State considers that this is likely to be because of a failure to report information` IS c
        `amount of employed earnings from the employment based on the information reported to HMRC and received by the Secretary of State from HMRC in the assessment period` IS reported
        `amount of employed earnings from the employment determined in accordance with regulation 55` IS 2100

-- A Real Time Information employer and no exception: what HMRC reported (1,800), or nil if nothing was received.
#ASSERT `reg 61(2) and (4) — the employed earnings from the employment for an assessment period` (`test employment` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE (JUST 1800)) EQUALS 1800
#ASSERT `reg 61(2) and (4) — the employed earnings from the employment for an assessment period` (`test employment` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE NOTHING) EQUALS 0
-- Each exception in (3) displaces the report: the amount determined under regulation 55 (2,100).
#ASSERT `reg 61(2) and (4) — the employed earnings from the employment for an assessment period` (`test employment` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE (JUST 1800)) EQUALS 2100
#ASSERT `reg 61(2) and (4) — the employed earnings from the employment for an assessment period` (`test employment` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE (JUST 1800)) EQUALS 2100
#ASSERT `reg 61(2) and (4) — the employed earnings from the employment for an assessment period` (`test employment` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE NOTHING) EQUALS 2100
-- Not a Real Time Information employer: regulation 55's amount.
#ASSERT `reg 61(2) and (4) — the employed earnings from the employment for an assessment period` (`test employment` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE (JUST 1800)) EQUALS 2100

GIVEN first IS A DATE
      last IS A DATE
GIVETH AN `Assessment period`
`test period` first last MEANS `Assessment period` WITH `first day` IS first, `last day` IS last

`test January period` MEANS `test period` (YearMonthDay 2026 1 5) (YearMonthDay 2026 2 4)
`test February period` MEANS `test period` (YearMonthDay 2026 2 5) (YearMonthDay 2026 3 4)
`test March period` MEANS `test period` (YearMonthDay 2026 3 5) (YearMonthDay 2026 4 4)

GIVEN late IS A BOOLEAN
      determined IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Payment of employed earnings that may have been reported late`
`test late payment` late determined MEANS
    `Payment of employed earnings that may have been reported late` WITH
        `the payment has been reported late, or otherwise reported in the wrong assessment period` IS late
        `the Secretary of State determines that the payment is to be treated as employed earnings in the assessment period in which it was received` IS determined
        `assessment period in which the payment was reported` IS `test February period`
        `assessment period in which the payment was received` IS `test January period`

-- (5): reported late and the Secretary of State so determines: the period of receipt (starting 5 January); otherwise the period reported (5 February).
#ASSERT (`reg 61(5) — the assessment period in which the payment is treated as employed earnings` (`test late payment` TRUE TRUE))'s `first day` EQUALS YearMonthDay 2026 1 5
#ASSERT (`reg 61(5) — the assessment period in which the payment is treated as employed earnings` (`test late payment` TRUE FALSE))'s `first day` EQUALS YearMonthDay 2026 2 5
#ASSERT (`reg 61(5) — the assessment period in which the payment is treated as employed earnings` (`test late payment` FALSE TRUE))'s `first day` EQUALS YearMonthDay 2026 2 5

GIVEN monthly IS A BOOLEAN
      several IS A BOOLEAN
      determined IS A BOOLEAN
      different IS A MAYBE `Assessment period`
GIVETH A `Regular monthly payment that may be moved to a different assessment period`
`test monthly payment` monthly several determined different MEANS
    `Regular monthly payment that may be moved to a different assessment period` WITH
        `the person is engaged in an employment where they are paid on a regular monthly basis` IS monthly
        `more than one payment in relation to that employment is reported in the same assessment period` IS several
        `the Secretary of State determines, for the purposes of maintaining a regular pattern, that one of those payments is to be treated as employed earnings in respect of a different assessment period` IS determined
        `assessment period in which the payment was reported` IS `test February period`
        `the different assessment period` IS different

-- (6): regular monthly pay, two payments reported in one period, and the Secretary of State moves one to March: the March period.
#ASSERT (`reg 61(6) — the assessment period in which one of the payments is treated as employed earnings` (`test monthly payment` TRUE TRUE TRUE (JUST `test March period`)))'s `first day` EQUALS YearMonthDay 2026 3 5
-- Each condition is needed.
#ASSERT (`reg 61(6) — the assessment period in which one of the payments is treated as employed earnings` (`test monthly payment` FALSE TRUE TRUE (JUST `test March period`)))'s `first day` EQUALS YearMonthDay 2026 2 5
#ASSERT (`reg 61(6) — the assessment period in which one of the payments is treated as employed earnings` (`test monthly payment` TRUE FALSE TRUE (JUST `test March period`)))'s `first day` EQUALS YearMonthDay 2026 2 5
#ASSERT (`reg 61(6) — the assessment period in which one of the payments is treated as employed earnings` (`test monthly payment` TRUE TRUE FALSE (JUST `test March period`)))'s `first day` EQUALS YearMonthDay 2026 2 5
-- No different period named: it stays in the period reported.
#ASSERT (`reg 61(6) — the assessment period in which one of the payments is treated as employed earnings` (`test monthly payment` TRUE TRUE TRUE NOTHING))'s `first day` EQUALS YearMonthDay 2026 2 5

-- (7): earnings 1,800 with a determination and a 150 adjustment: 1,950; without a determination the adjustment is not made.
#ASSERT `reg 61(7) — the employed earnings after any consequential adjustment` 1800 TRUE 150 EQUALS 1950
#ASSERT `reg 61(7) — the employed earnings after any consequential adjustment` 1800 TRUE (0 MINUS 150) EQUALS 1650
#ASSERT `reg 61(7) — the employed earnings after any consequential adjustment` 1800 FALSE 150 EQUALS 1800
